{'symbol': 'GM', 'date': '2022-04-05 10:04:00', 'title': "GM AND HONDA WILL CODEVELOP AFFORDABLE EVS TARGETING THE WORLD'S MOST POPULAR VEHICLE SEGMENTS", 'text': "NEW EV SERIES EXPECTED TO GO ON SALE IN 2027 STARTING IN NORTH AMERICA HONDA AND GM COLLABORATION DESIGNED TO ENABLE GLOBAL PRODUCTION OF MILLIONS OF EVS COMPANIES WILL EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES \xa0FOR ADVANCED BATTERY COLLABORATION DETROIT AND TOKYO , APRIL 5, 2022 /PRNEWSWIRE/ -- GENERAL MOTORS (NYSE: GM) AND HONDA TODAY ANNOUNCED PLANS TO EXPAND THE TWO COMPANIES' RELATIONSHIP TO A NEW CHAPTER BY CODEVELOPING A SERIES OF AFFORDABLE ELECTRIC VEHICLES BASED ON A NEW GLOBAL ARCHITECTURE USING NEXT-GENERATION ULTIUM BATTERY TECHNOLOGY.\xa0 THE COMPANIES ARE WORKING TOGETHER TO ENABLE GLOBAL PRODUCTION\xa0OF MILLIONS OF EVS STARTING IN 2027, INCLUDING COMPACT CROSSOVER VEHICLES, LEVERAGING THE TWO COMPANIES' TECHNOLOGY, DESIGN AND SOURCING STRATEGIES."}